<!--Post: 285--><!--Time: 1087227351-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST285"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Swa<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Swa<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, June 14, 2004 - 8:35 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->This case has puzzled me ever since I started reading about it a little over a month ago.  Just when you think you can lead yourself to a conclusion -- you read another piece of evidence that discounts what you thought. <BR> <BR>I just can&#39;t believe that there has been no SERIOUS leads or breakthroughs ever made in this case.   At least in other high profile cases like Zodiac -- we can pretty much assume who it was eventhough we may never know. <BR> <BR>With BTK -- We really have had no SERIOUS names to associate this with.  I still don&#39;t understand many of the decisions made by the police department either. <BR> <BR>I mean we&#39;re talking about a three mile radius that he worked in?  He&#39;d walk around in camoflauge clothing?  Why was it so hard to catch this guy?  I mean we&#39;re talking about someone who OBVIOUSLY knows the area like the back of his hand. <BR> <BR>The phone call also is puzzling.  No one in the Wichita vicinity could recognize the voice -- eventhough this guy obviously lived in the area.  This makes you think that maybe HE DID have some sort of modulator to disguise his voice.  The way he pronounced his &#34;O&#39;s&#34; just wasn&#39;t the norm I&#39;m sure for that area of the country. <BR> <BR>I am hoping they catch him soon just so we can see what kind of person gave the Wichita Police so much trouble for 30 years.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 285-->
<!--Post: 288--><!--Time: 1087233159-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST288"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Warren_b<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Warren_b<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, June 14, 2004 - 10:12 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Swa, I believe the paucity of suspects is due solely to WPD&#39;s  failure to release any meaningful information &#40;the phone call being the exception&#41;about the murders. Again, the failure to release the fact that Bright&#39;s attacker wore a camoflauge jacket is simply unbelievable. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 288-->
<!--Post: 292--><!--Time: 1087248902-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST292"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Swa<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Swa<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, June 14, 2004 - 2:35 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Warren -- <BR> <BR>What do you think the main reason is they won&#39;t release any information?   I think they could release &#34;enough&#34; information without leaking important deatils like a signature calling card, etc.. so copycats won&#39;t appear. <BR> <BR>After 30 years you&#39;d think they show their hand so someone might have some useful information. <BR> <BR>Even releasing the phone call AFTER the fact shows a serious level of incompetence. <BR> <BR>The WPD sort of reminds me of what would happen if there would have been a murder in Mayberry.. Wait.. Andy Griffith would have found the guy... Bad example.. <IMG SRC="http://www.catchbtk.com/discus/clipart/happy.gif" ALT=":-&#41;" BORDER=0> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 292-->
<!--Post: 295--><!--Time: 1087283286-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST295"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Louise<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Louise<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, June 15, 2004 - 12:08 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Something tells me that there are enough &#34;copycats&#34; out there, and that BTK himself is so zealously craving attention, that LE has had to distance themselves from releasing critical information...something also tells me that they are hot on a couple of trails and, like a cat watching a bird in a tree, don&#39;t want anyone making waves...for some reason, perhaps evidence they are still seeking, they don&#39;t have enough of an airtight case to arrest him?! But I just don&#39;t think they&#39;re as emptyhanded as it seems.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 295-->
<!--Post: 296--><!--Time: 1087286147-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST296"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Louise<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Louise<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, June 15, 2004 - 12:55 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->What leads me to the conclusion that LE has some hot leads? Notice how they have gone silent...right after the letters they were begging the public for information and leads. I think they are rich with leads right now and cannot reveal any of it to us...that would be like giving the clues to the perpetrator! If they were desperate we would probably hear from them.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 296-->
<!--Post: 306--><!--Time: 1087845899-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST306"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Screamer<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Screamer<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, June 21, 2004 - 12:24 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Louise, I hope that is the case, but IMO I think that LE are no closer than they were in 1974. This has frustrated me for years. I certainly hope that I&#39;m wrong and they catch this guy.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 306-->
